    "created_at": "2016-03-10T09:36:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-10T09:36:11Z",
    "body": "When the WebSockets were being introduced, people at HyBi worried much about it being abused for cross-protocol attacks. IIRC, it's a part of outcome of discussion on such concerns.\n\nThe Blink side implementation of this was done in 2009 for WebKit based on the spec text in WHATWG spec.\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/37942cd0eaf481d2c52ddc30427683a5c9535752%5E%21/\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=32085\nThe list was taken from http://www-archive.mozilla.org/projects/netlib/PortBanning.html.\n\nIn Chromium, the HTTP stack also blocks access to ports for the same set of known legacy protocols as WebSockets. So, adding this requirement to Fetch would make itself close to our policy.\nhttps://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/net/base/port_util.cc&l=22\n\nThis list was already there since the initial commit of Chromium repo (2008-07-26). Maybe it's from the same source (Mozilla's one).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
